<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch manufacturing output seen higher.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch manufacturing output seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect manufacturing production figures for February due on Friday to be substantionally higher compared with January.</p>
<p>They forecast that the seasonally adjusted month-on-month figure will rise by 1.2 to 3.5 percent compared to a drop of 3.4 percent in the previous month.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date-Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0730 18/4 Febr   Manufac. output M/M   2.5 pct    1.2/3.5  -3.4</p>
<p> 0870 18/4 Febr   Manufac. output Y/Y   3.7 pct    2.5/5.0   0.5</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
